            <ArticleTitle>Relaxation therapy: its potential as an intervention for acute postoperative pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Given the complexity of pain processes, pain relief requires a creative and varied approach. Professional and governmental groups are supporting a holistic approach to pain that results in more positive outcomes for patients. Relaxation techniques provide clients with a strategy for reducing the stress, anxiety, and muscle tension related to pain. Understanding pain, anxiety, and relaxation provides the postanesthesia nurse with an alternative, nonpharmacological method of pain management.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
